 "text": "The Band-Aid was invented out of love. Around 1920, New Jersey, Earle Dickson works for Johnson & Johnson. His wife, Josephine, keeps cutting and burning her fingers in the kitchen. Regular bandages fall right off. So Earle puts small squares of gauze down a long strip of tape so she can cut one off and fix herself, even when he's not home. His boss loves it. In 1921, Band-Aids go on sale. Every legend has a beginning.",
